pocket-motion-only: the framebuffer here is read back as RGBA and handed to codecs and PNGs that carry an alpha plane; every upstream target presents an opaque surface — the RGB565 hosts have no alpha byte and the ARGB blit path composites straight onto a screen — so a transparent clear buys them nothing and costs a per-pixel branch in blend.

0014 — the framebuffer carries alpha: a frame clears to TRANSPARENT black
instead of opaque black, and a partial source over a partially covered
destination composites straight-alpha src-over in colour and alpha.

Over an opaque destination the arithmetic is the expression the buffer always
used, verbatim, so a composition that declares a ground renders byte for byte
as before — the digest ledger is the check, and `compositions/alpha` is the
one entry that moves. What changes is a pixel no op reached (alpha 0 where it
was 255) and a pixel reached only with partial alpha (its own colour with the
coverage in the alpha byte, where it was that colour mixed toward black under
a 255).

By file:
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: `RenderTarget::fill_clear` and `clear`
  (opaque black by default, zero bytes for `RgbaTarget`); `clear_rect` on the
  incremental path; `RgbaTarget::blend` branches on destination alpha and
  keeps the old expression for 255; `Masked` delegates the clear to its inner
  target. The RGB565 targets are untouched.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs` and the tests in `raster.rs`: four new tests —
  a transparent clear with an opaque box, a 50% box over transparent keeping
  its colour, a declared ground opaque everywhere and blending as before, two
  50% layers composing src-over. Nine existing assertions that read the clear
  as opaque black are updated; three of them by declaring the black ground
  they were written against, so coverage still reads as luminance.

Red case: with the general blend path replaced by the opaque expression,
`half_alpha_box_over_transparent_keeps_its_colour`,
`two_half_alpha_layers_over_transparent_compose_src_over` and
`textures_and_font_coverage_are_sampled_at_physical_resolution` fail.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

